ii) after evaluation of the evidence on record, the learned trial Judge  R/CR.A/470/2013 JUDGMENT DATED: 08/08/2022 has come to the conclusion that there is breach of provisions of Rule 14 of the Rules;
iii) it is also revealed from the record that date of packing of the sample in question was 06.12.2003, for which, the bill was dated 01.08.2003 thus, the bill was of prior to the date of packing;
iv) referring to the deposition of the complainant, it is also observed by the learned trial Judge that so far as breach of Rule 50 is concerned, it is revealed that the complainant had not called for from the respondent Nos. 1 and 2 the licence as per Rule 50 of the Rules and accordingly, the sanction relating to breach of Rule 50 becomes invalid;
v) the standard of proof in criminal cases is beyond reasonable doubt.
